1
00:00:06,864 --> 00:00:09,233
Whiskers and the Painted Wall.

2
00:00:18,409 --> 00:00:22,804
One morning, there was only one warm sunbeam on the windowsill.

3
00:00:28,812 --> 00:00:30,920
My sunbeam! I was here first.

4
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:33,612
You were snoring on the rug! I was here first!

5
00:00:40,676 --> 00:00:43,120
There. A wall. My side. Your side.

6
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:45,592
Oh dear. A wall between best friends.

7
00:00:51,072 --> 00:00:54,108
Look! That moving van is going all the way to Berlin!

8
00:00:54,308 --> 00:00:56,399
Then I'm going to Berlin. Alone!

9
00:00:56,599 --> 00:00:58,341
Me too. Also alone!

10
00:01:05,405 --> 00:01:06,446
Wait for me!

11
00:01:11,926 --> 00:01:16,695
All night the van rumbled on, with a wall of boxes between the cats.

12
00:01:22,175 --> 00:01:24,780
Pip. Tell Luna it's cold on my side.

13
00:01:29,204 --> 00:01:30,930
Luna, he says he's cold.

14
00:01:31,130 --> 00:01:33,064
Tell him it's cold on my side too.

15
00:01:37,488 --> 00:01:39,526
Why not sit together? It's warmer.

16
00:01:39,726 --> 00:01:40,401
Never!

17
00:01:40,601 --> 00:01:41,413
Never!

18
00:01:52,173 --> 00:01:54,170
Next morning: Berlin!

19
00:01:54,370 --> 00:01:57,359
Hallo! Willkommen! I'm Berti, the Berlin bear.

20
00:01:57,559 --> 00:02:01,379
The bear is on Berlin's flag, you know. Come, I'll show you my city!

21
00:02:08,971 --> 00:02:12,939
The Brandenburg Gate! On top, four horses pull a chariot.

22
00:02:13,139 --> 00:02:15,600
Do the horses ever get a snack break?

23
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:19,275
Long ago, a wall stood here. Nobody could pass through.

24
00:02:27,923 --> 00:02:30,674
Whiskers' nose found a snack stand.

25
00:02:30,874 --> 00:02:34,547
Guten Tag! Pretzels, currywurst, and fresh Berliner doughnuts!

26
00:02:34,747 --> 00:02:37,045
One of everything! For me only.

27
00:02:44,637 --> 00:02:46,472
He's wearing it like a necklace!

28
00:02:46,672 --> 00:02:49,723
I did that on purpose. It's a travel snack.

29
00:02:56,259 --> 00:02:57,102
Whiskers!

30
00:02:57,302 --> 00:02:59,100
Not on purpose! Really!

31
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:01,875
Come, Pip. We're taking the train. Without him.

32
00:03:06,299 --> 00:03:11,623
Berlin's yellow trains even cross the river, on a bridge with red towers.

33
00:03:18,687 --> 00:03:19,856
Luna! Wait!

34
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:29,392
Don't worry! We'll follow along the river.

35
00:03:34,872 --> 00:03:38,848
Along the river stood a long wall, covered in paintings.

36
00:03:39,048 --> 00:03:42,642
Artists from everywhere. It's a piece of the old Berlin Wall.

37
00:03:42,842 --> 00:03:46,614
For years it kept friends apart. When it fell, everyone hugged.

38
00:03:46,814 --> 00:03:49,305
Then they painted it with happy pictures.

39
00:03:57,953 --> 00:04:02,094
I built a wall this morning. Out of cushions. Now I'm lonely.

40
00:04:05,462 --> 00:04:07,593
Then paint something. Right here.

41
00:04:17,297 --> 00:04:18,766
Whiskers? Is that us?

42
00:04:18,966 --> 00:04:22,707
Luna! I'm sorry. The sunbeam is big enough for two.

43
00:04:22,907 --> 00:04:25,718
I'm sorry too. I missed you, you big furry grump.

44
00:04:32,254 --> 00:04:33,972
Hooray! The wall is down!

45
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:40,374
That evening, they rode up the TV Tower.

46
00:04:47,438 --> 00:04:49,096
Whee! My ears went pop!

47
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:55,851
Look! The Gate, the glass dome, the river!

48
00:04:56,051 --> 00:04:59,622
Once, from up here, you could see the wall cut the city in two.

49
00:04:59,822 --> 00:05:01,929
Now there's just one Berlin.

50
00:05:02,129 --> 00:05:04,953
One Berlin. And one sunbeam, for two.

51
00:05:18,881 --> 00:05:21,537
The empty van carried them home.

52
00:05:25,961 --> 00:05:27,805
Whiskers! What happened to your wall?

53
00:05:28,005 --> 00:05:31,086
I knocked it down. Now it's a bed. For two.

54
00:05:31,286 --> 00:05:34,136
And I brought one pretzel from Berlin. For sharing.

55
00:05:34,336 --> 00:05:36,381
Then I'll share. On purpose.

56
00:05:40,805 --> 00:05:45,824
Walls keep friends apart. But one little sorry can bring any wall down.

